## Executive Summary
April’s petrol price surge in South Africa is the steepest in recent history, with **diesel and paraffin seeing record increases**—affecting affordability for households and businesses. The hike reflects a combination of global supply constraints and government tax adjustments.

---

## Price Impact by Fuel Type
Below are the projected price changes, highlighting the highest impacts:

| Fuel Type       | Inland Price (R) | Coastal Price (R) | Increase (R) |
|-----------------|---------------|----------------|--------------|
| Diesel           | R 28.67        | R 27.83         | **+10.13**   |
| Paraffin        | R 24.17        | R 23.16         | **+11.63**   |
| **95 Petrol**   | R 26.12        | R 25.29         | **+5.82**    |
| **93 Petrol**   | R 25.50        | R 24.67         | **+5.31**

*These figures reflect projected inland/coastal prices, including global supply constraints and local tax adjustments (21c/litre petrol, 23c/litre diesel).*

---

## Key Economic Impact
- **Diesel users**: Face a **R10+ increase**, worsening transport costs for commuters and businesses.
- **Paraffin consumers**: See a **R11+ jump**, impacting heating/lighting budgets for households.
- **Global + Local Factors**: Supply constraints and tax hikes (21c/litre petrol, 23c/litre diesel) drive these record increases.

---

## When to Expect Changes
The official price changes will take effect at midnight on **Wednesday, April 1, 2026**. Fill up before this date for the latest rates.

